      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Kraftvaerk.Umbraco.Headless.CacheKeys"
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "2fbb5f26-eb3b-443e-80ac-5699dcbab4ea",
      "key": "d6204b51-a451-45f4-a091-028e47fe5227",
      "values": []
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "393273e2-6c41-4db8-8d6f-3efe33e66f1b",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EKraftvaerk.Umbraco.Headless.CacheKeys enhances the Umbraco Delivery API by adding a cacheKeys field to content responses, making it easier to implement efficient caching and precise invalidation strategies for headless frontends. It automatically tracks dependencies across content and media, ensuring pages can be invalidated when related items change. The package also extends the OpenAPI (Swagger) schema for better tooling support and developer experience. With built-in support for recursive child keys, it\u2019s especially useful for listings like blogs or news pages, helping keep headless sites fast and responsive.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EThis particular piece of content has the following cache keys:\u003C/strong\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "9ede4277-930d-4106-b18c-b3380269d981",
      "key": "4f20ccfb-4978-448a-a3fa-8124280eede2",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Kraftvaerk.Umbraco.Headless.BlockPreview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a34c3bf8-3b46-4f88-9bb0-09b0ed11c963",
      "key": "ef8e0750-dba9-41bd-97d4-ac95cb73fef5",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "iconImage",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "1072e7c3-4deb-4904-ba7b-c9d7330fe4b8",
              "mediaKey": "3102b530-00ce-426b-8bb8-b8623b01fbdc",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELive preview of your blocks, right inside the backoffice \u2014 powered by your frontend.\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\u003Ca target=\u0022\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/kraftvaerk/kraftvaerk.umbraco.headless.blockpreview\u0022 title=\u0022github.com\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EGo to Github\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "header",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Block Preview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "37af3f54-4f3f-47ea-858e-9556f6e7c9cf",
      "key": "fa25d94a-0b41-48c8-88d7-ec98623af129",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "url",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "https://player.vimeo.com/video/1113541903?badge=0\u0026amp;autopause=0\u0026amp;player_id=0\u0026amp;app_id=58479"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "c18a26c5-f4f6-484a-8a7a-35a0b88ece0f",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EKraftvaerk.Umbraco.Headless.BlockPreview brings live, inline previews of blocks directly into the Umbraco backoffice, powered by your frontend. \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESupporting Block List, Block Grid, and RTE blocks, it lets editors see real rendered HTML while they edit, using your existing headless setup (Vue, React, Razor, or anything else). It\u2019s multi-site and culture-aware, with settings persisted in blockPreview/state.json so you can commit and share configurations across environments. Flexible and fully configurable, BlockPreview gives developers full control over how previews are rendered, while giving editors a smoother, more intuitive editing experience.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIf that doesn\u0027t explain it well enough, watch the (silent) video beneath.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "9ede4277-930d-4106-b18c-b3380269d981",
      "key": "f9c10ddd-521d-4933-b3fc-030f6ff36ce1",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "headerTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Kraftvaerk.Umbraco.Blockfilter "
        },
        {
          "alias": "headerLevel",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            "H2"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "a34c3bf8-3b46-4f88-9bb0-09b0ed11c963",
      "key": "fd4fcd0a-5979-4172-8f25-578ea62eaac0",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "iconImage",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "be53b42c-eef1-4f1d-b39d-7bffd52c78f2",
              "mediaKey": "c6d57354-e8ea-41aa-a631-3a6be66c11f4",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBlock Filter is a simple package that replaces the Block Catalogue Modal in Umbraco with one under our control.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEver wished a block could only be available to certain users or user groups? Only on certain pages? Only if the editor alias is gridContent? Or maybe only if the logged-in user\u2019s first name is Unicorn?\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca target=\u0022_blank\u0022 data-router-slot=\u0022disabled\u0022 href=\u0022https://github.com/kraftvaerk/kraftvaerk.umbraco.blockfilter\u0022 title=\u0022github.com\u0022 type=\u0022external\u0022\u003EGo to Github\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "header",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Block Filter"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "387fbbea-8c41-4019-ac76-c3e6e590f6e1",
      "key": "b63ca474-2eba-43d4-882e-37ac5a2c09c0",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "richText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp class=\u0022text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)\u0022\u003EBlock Filter (by Kraftvaerk) is an open-source Umbraco package that gives developers full control over the Block Catalogue Modal. By using the RemodelBlockCatalogueNotification, you can decide exactly which blocks should be available \u2014 whether based on user groups, content types, editor aliases, or even custom conditions. Compatible with Umbraco 16.0\u002B, it\u2019s easy to install via NuGet and extend with your own notification handlers. With Block Filter, you define who sees what, ensuring a tailored and flexible editing experience.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EKjeldsen.dev currently runs with this nonsense - allowing only the cache key example block above (with the table) to be inserted on this page.\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "f618abe7-aaac-4ad7-927c-4d39b15c975d",
      "key": "541ef833-497c-436b-b32f-df196b05cc11",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "code",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "\u0060\u0060\u0060csharp\r\npublic class YourNotificationHandler : INotificationAsyncHandler\u003CRemodelBlockCatalogueNotification\u003E\r\n{\r\n    private readonly IContentService _contentService;\r\n    public YourNotificationHandler(IContentService contentService)\r\n    {\r\n        _contentService = contentService;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    public async Task HandleAsync(\r\n        RemodelBlockCatalogueNotification notification, \r\n        CancellationToken cancellationToken)\r\n    {\r\n        var id = notification.Model.ContentId;\r\n\r\n        if(id == null)\r\n        {\r\n            return;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        var name = _contentService.GetById(Guid.Parse(id)).Name;\r\n        \r\n        if(!name.Equals(\u0022umbraco packages\u0022, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))\r\n        {\r\n            notification.Model.Blocks =\r\n                notification.Model.Blocks\r\n                .Where(x =\u003E x.Alias != \u0022cacheKeyExampleBlock\u0022).ToList();\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\npublic class YourComposer : IComposer\r\n{\r\n    public void Compose(IUmbracoBuilder builder)\r\n    {\r\n        builder.\r\n            AddNotificationAsyncHandler\u003CRemodelBlockCatalogueNotification, YourNotificationHandler\u003E();\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\u0060\u0060\u0060"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
